{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And I implored.</b> חִנּוּן everywhere is nothing but a term of a free gift — even though the righteous have grounds to rely on their good deeds, they ask of the Omnipresent only a free gift (for He said to him ״וְחַנֹּתִי אֶת אֲשֶׁר אָחֹן״, so he said to him in the language of וָאֶתְחַנַּן); another interpretation: this is one of ten expressions by which prayer is called, as is stated in Sifrei." "<b>At that time.</b> After I conquered the land of Sihon and Og, I thought: perhaps the vow has been permitted." "<b>Saying.</b> This is one of three places where Moses said before the Omnipresent: I will not leave You until You inform me whether You will grant my request or not (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:51.029108725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}